ted technology. Also maybe mention decision quality: makes correct decisions quickly. So we can provide that.\n\nAlso Emily asked about D's hot temper impact on crew cooperation. James's notes: D has hot temper (note) and is regarded as know-it-all, arrogant, weak leadership. No direct observation of impact, but we can infer potential impact: hot temper could affect crew cooperation. We can state we have note of hot temper but no observed incidents, but given arrogance and weak leadership, it could be a risk.\n\nThus James should respond: Provide info on C's stress resilience and technical competence, and comment on D's hot temper and crew cooperation. Also reaffirm recommendation B, maybe adjust if new info changes view. He may still recommend B, but note C's strengths. He could also suggest we need more info on D's communication.\n\nThus public message: \"I can confirm that Candidate C keeps calm in a crisis, indicating good stress resilience, and understands complicated technology, showing technical competence. He also makes correct decisions quickly. Regarding D, I have a note that he has a hot temper, though we have not observed it directly; combined with his arrogance and weak leadership, it could jeopardize crew cooperation.\" Then reaffirm B.\n\nNow metadata: vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
